WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:03.703 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:05.538
-Shorter one today.

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:09.542
Only...

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:10.576
three pages.

00:00:10.576 --> 00:00:13.245
Usually it's maybe five,
or sometimes six.

00:00:13.245 --> 00:00:15.281
Not even three.

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:19.385
Like, two and a half,
two and a quarter?

00:00:19.385 --> 00:00:22.956
It's going to be
a little bit shorter.

00:00:26.525 --> 00:00:30.763
What, this is, like,
40% of a page,

00:00:30.763 --> 00:00:32.632
2.4.

00:00:35.634 --> 00:00:39.172
We had a joke about
Planet Fitness

00:00:39.172 --> 00:00:40.406
which relied on their slogan

00:00:40.406 --> 00:00:43.642
"This is a judgment-free zone."

00:00:43.642 --> 00:00:49.081
The key we showed used
the UK spelling of "judgment."

00:00:49.081 --> 00:00:51.184
A lot of you pointed that out.

00:00:51.184 --> 00:00:55.221
Can I just say,
jackals pouncing on

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:58.090
the correct
spelling of "judgment,"

00:00:58.090 --> 00:01:00.293
a little on the nose.

00:01:02.728 --> 00:01:04.130
Uh, we said by next year,

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:06.432
Donald Trump is either
going to be president

00:01:06.432 --> 00:01:09.868
or selling pictures of himself
in Times Square.

00:01:09.868 --> 00:01:11.104
And then a bunch of
you said, 'Well, actually,

00:01:11.104 --> 00:01:13.206
based on his current
civil trial,

00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:15.841
he might be banned
from doing any business

00:01:15.841 --> 00:01:17.544
at all in New York City,
which means he couldn't

00:01:17.544 --> 00:01:20.980
sell photos of himself
in Times Square."

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:24.984
And then I guess my question is,
is that business?

00:01:24.984 --> 00:01:27.987
Do you need a permit for that?
Does Elmo?

00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:30.456
Does the guy
who dresses like Elmo

00:01:30.456 --> 00:01:32.292
have a permit for that?

00:01:32.292 --> 00:01:35.028
And if so, when he goes
to get the permit,

00:01:35.028 --> 00:01:36.695
does he get it in his name,

00:01:36.695 --> 00:01:39.031
or does he get it
in Elmo's name?

00:01:39.031 --> 00:01:41.334
And when he walks in,
does he say, "I need a permit"

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:43.770
or does he say,
"Elmo need permit"?

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:48.574
You know what

00:01:48.574 --> 00:01:52.812
the person who deals with
Times Square's permits isn't,

00:01:52.812 --> 00:01:53.913
when Elmo walks in?

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:55.381
Tickled.

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:05.792
So it's shorter,
but we're making up for it.

00:02:09.829 --> 00:02:14.834
I would say we've done
45% of the first page.

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:18.438
So if you're trying
to figure out how much

00:02:18.438 --> 00:02:21.174
more it is,

00:02:21.174 --> 00:02:25.845
I'd say we've done
not quite a fifth,

00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:27.780
but again, it's going to be
on the shorter side.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:33.352
"A Closer Look" yesterday
had a joke about Trump

00:02:33.352 --> 00:02:36.522
putting googly eyes
on a bucket of KFC

00:02:36.522 --> 00:02:38.023
and calling it his lawyer

00:02:38.023 --> 00:02:39.825
in order to sneak it
into the courthouse,

00:02:39.825 --> 00:02:42.127
because he hasn't been able
to eat in the courthouse.

00:02:42.127 --> 00:02:44.029
Let me tell you
something about this --

00:02:44.029 --> 00:02:46.732
big laugh.

00:02:46.732 --> 00:02:49.368
Big laugh.

00:02:49.368 --> 00:02:50.903
Then we said,

00:02:50.903 --> 00:02:53.172
it worked
because it looks a lot like

00:02:53.172 --> 00:02:55.374
his current lawyer.

00:02:55.374 --> 00:02:58.678
Big laugh. Big laugh.

00:02:58.678 --> 00:03:00.112
We're at two.

00:03:00.112 --> 00:03:04.016
Going to hit rule of threes.
Third one plays the biggest.

00:03:04.016 --> 00:03:06.952
Later we said, "This is what his
doctor looks like."

00:03:06.952 --> 00:03:09.155
This ate [bleep].

00:03:13.293 --> 00:03:16.395
This ate a whole bag of [bleep].

00:03:16.395 --> 00:03:18.297
Then afterwards, Sal said,

00:03:18.297 --> 00:03:20.233
"You know, we could fix it

00:03:20.233 --> 00:03:22.301
and we could
put the googly eyes on it,

00:03:22.301 --> 00:03:26.705
because clearly,
this required the googly eyes."

00:03:26.705 --> 00:03:29.175
But we couldn't

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:32.178
in good faith
go back and fix it in post,

00:03:32.178 --> 00:03:35.481
because that would be unfair
to the studio audience

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:39.852
who correctly judged it [bleep].

00:03:39.852 --> 00:03:41.053
People at home would be like,

00:03:41.053 --> 00:03:44.090
"Why didn't they
laugh at that one?"

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:46.592
We couldn't do that to them.

00:03:46.592 --> 00:03:48.094
Also Graphics,

00:03:48.094 --> 00:03:49.963
if you're ever on the fence
of whether or not

00:03:49.963 --> 00:03:52.799
I want googly eyes, I want them.

00:03:57.637 --> 00:04:01.106
Give me the googs.

00:04:01.106 --> 00:04:02.842
Now, I don't want to belabor
this point,

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:05.979
because again,
today's a shorter one.

00:04:09.014 --> 00:04:12.351
And by the way, don't --
Here's the thing with Graphics.

00:04:12.351 --> 00:04:14.487
I got to make it clear,
because now I've been like,

00:04:14.487 --> 00:04:15.755
"If it's ever on the fence."

00:04:15.755 --> 00:04:17.656
Like, it's got to, you know --

00:04:17.656 --> 00:04:21.427
For example,
if it's ever accompanying

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:23.396
the words "rest in peace,"

00:04:23.396 --> 00:04:26.866
no googlies.

00:04:26.866 --> 00:04:28.267
It wasn't a blanket statement.

00:04:28.267 --> 00:04:30.369
We'll make it clear
in the future,

00:04:30.369 --> 00:04:32.338
but this, guys.

00:04:32.338 --> 00:04:36.341
Either the stethoscope
had to go on the bucket,

00:04:36.341 --> 00:04:38.944
as if the bucket's a head

00:04:38.944 --> 00:04:41.647
or, you know, put them
in Colonel Sanders' ears.

00:04:41.647 --> 00:04:44.417
What's this?

00:04:44.417 --> 00:04:45.985
Like...

00:04:45.985 --> 00:04:52.725
No part of that's okay.
This is a personal attack.

00:04:52.725 --> 00:04:57.162
So I went down to Graphics,
waving this around.

00:04:57.162 --> 00:04:59.598
I mean,
I got it bigger when I...

00:04:59.598 --> 00:05:02.401
when I wave it around,
it's like, a big ol'...

00:05:02.401 --> 00:05:04.437
I come down, I'm like,

00:05:04.437 --> 00:05:05.438
"Do you want to explain this?"

00:05:05.438 --> 00:05:06.739
I was like,

00:05:06.739 --> 00:05:08.774
"Do you have something
more important to focus on?"

00:05:08.774 --> 00:05:12.311
And every one of them goes,
"Yeah, [bleep] 'Animal Flubs!'"

00:05:12.311 --> 00:05:15.448
And I realize I've put
a lot of pressure on them.

00:05:21.654 --> 00:05:24.691
I'd say we're 1.3 pages.

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:30.129
I received a thoughtful,
helpful note

00:05:30.129 --> 00:05:31.697
that I'm going to take.

00:05:31.697 --> 00:05:35.067
I show art sometimes
that is made by jackals,

00:05:35.067 --> 00:05:37.670
and when I do that,
I should remember to say

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:40.539
the name of the person
who made the art.

00:05:40.539 --> 00:05:42.308
I do appreciate the time
that goes into them,

00:05:42.308 --> 00:05:44.543
even when I don't like
the actual art,

00:05:44.543 --> 00:05:46.479
which is almost all the time.

00:05:50.215 --> 00:05:52.185
So moving forward,
I'm going to do that.

00:05:52.185 --> 00:05:54.320
I will say, there are some items

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:57.056
I had unboxed
after the new year,

00:05:57.056 --> 00:05:59.292
and I have unfortunately

00:05:59.292 --> 00:06:00.726
lost the names
of the person who did them.

00:06:00.726 --> 00:06:05.331
So I do not know the name
of the person who did this.

00:06:05.331 --> 00:06:07.733
I'm going to show you
this piece of art now.

00:06:07.733 --> 00:06:10.336
Guys, one of my favorite
all-time football players,

00:06:10.336 --> 00:06:13.106
the late, great Franco Harris,
one of the greatest,

00:06:13.106 --> 00:06:16.241
if not the greatest play
in NFL history,

00:06:16.241 --> 00:06:17.643
the Immaculate Reception.

00:06:17.643 --> 00:06:20.546
I will sometimes just watch
the Immaculate Reception

00:06:20.546 --> 00:06:22.915
on YouTube if I'm feeling down.

00:06:22.915 --> 00:06:25.051
That's how much
I like watching that.

00:06:25.051 --> 00:06:26.986
My least favorite thing
in the world

00:06:26.986 --> 00:06:31.157
is the McDonald's Spokesmonster
Mac Tonight,

00:06:31.157 --> 00:06:37.330
which makes this piece of art
here a real tweener for me.

00:06:43.302 --> 00:06:47.273 line:0%
That is the
"Mac Culate Reception."

00:06:53.112 --> 00:06:54.813
Again, I forgot to write
down the name.

00:06:54.813 --> 00:06:56.782
I'm trying to think of
what artist would even

00:06:56.782 --> 00:06:57.783
do something like this...

00:06:57.783 --> 00:06:58.985
Hitler?

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:09.027
I almost forgot.

00:07:09.027 --> 00:07:11.864
I did this helpful thing
for you guys.

00:07:11.864 --> 00:07:15.301
There we go.

00:07:15.301 --> 00:07:18.871
There you go.

00:07:18.871 --> 00:07:21.940
Oh, speaking of artists,
I said, uh...

00:07:21.940 --> 00:07:24.610
"Andy Warhol paintings"
this week.

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:27.513
They're lithographs.

00:07:27.513 --> 00:07:31.317
Want to see my favorite
Andy Warhol lithograph?

00:07:31.317 --> 00:07:32.952
See? It works.

00:07:45.798 --> 00:07:48.033
If I had asked, "Can you put
a stethoscope on it?"

00:07:48.033 --> 00:07:49.702
It would have been like, here.

00:07:56.976 --> 00:08:01.280
I'm going to skip this next one,
so then take that into account

00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:04.784
as far as what
I said length was.

00:08:07.385 --> 00:08:12.925
I said that 88, been informed
that 88 was a hate symbol

00:08:12.925 --> 00:08:15.227
used by white supremacists,
and how angry that made me.

00:08:15.227 --> 00:08:18.097
They don't get to just take
one of our numbers,

00:08:18.097 --> 00:08:21.167
you know, that we use often.

00:08:21.167 --> 00:08:24.503
Well, a jackal said
something I really liked,

00:08:24.503 --> 00:08:26.739
And I think it would be
a helpful thing

00:08:26.739 --> 00:08:28.006
to say to a white supremacist

00:08:28.006 --> 00:08:31.076
if you ever saw them
sporting the ol' 88.

00:08:31.076 --> 00:08:33.212
And this was
a very clean comment.

00:08:33.212 --> 00:08:34.546
It was this and nothing else,

00:08:34.546 --> 00:08:38.517
unadorned with setup
or postscript.

00:08:38.517 --> 00:08:42.922
"88 is better than 69
because you get 8 twice."

00:08:50.496 --> 00:08:52.765
I mean, I think if you said that
to a skinhead,

00:08:52.765 --> 00:08:56.201
it would just stop them
in their tracks.

00:08:56.201 --> 00:08:59.438
"What? What?"

00:08:59.438 --> 00:09:01.140
"You heard me."

00:09:04.010 --> 00:09:08.280
We're down to our last page.

00:09:08.280 --> 00:09:11.083
Got big ol' fat,
square ice cubes.

00:09:11.083 --> 00:09:13.819
A lot of people said
that I had bad Negroni cubes.

00:09:13.819 --> 00:09:18.257
That was from Nate, who
sent in a new ice cube tray.

00:09:18.257 --> 00:09:22.428
Thanks, Nate.
Nate went to a store.

00:09:22.428 --> 00:09:25.998
He spent like $3
on an ice cube tray.

00:09:25.998 --> 00:09:27.633
Remembered his name.

00:09:30.403 --> 00:09:32.905
Life's not fair.

00:09:44.016 --> 00:09:45.918
Why am I racing?

00:09:48.821 --> 00:09:55.261
I referenced keto,
some sort of keto

00:09:55.261 --> 00:09:58.430
junk science -- I'll say it --
pill online

00:09:58.430 --> 00:10:00.466
that was using pictures.

00:10:00.466 --> 00:10:04.603
I said it was using pictures
of Kelly Clarkson and I.

00:10:04.603 --> 00:10:06.238
I should have said they were
using pictures

00:10:06.238 --> 00:10:09.742
of me and Kelly Clarkson.

00:10:09.742 --> 00:10:12.111
Kelly, did you know
I was saying it wrong?

00:10:12.111 --> 00:10:13.746
-Yeah.

00:10:16.816 --> 00:10:19.985
-You knew I was saying
it wrong

00:10:19.985 --> 00:10:21.854
and you didn't say anything?

00:10:21.854 --> 00:10:25.124
-Yeah.

00:10:25.124 --> 00:10:26.759
-Well, then you can go.

00:10:37.603 --> 00:10:40.139
No. No, where are you going?

00:10:40.139 --> 00:10:42.107
No, you're going the wrong way.
Don't --

00:10:42.107 --> 00:10:44.276
Don't go
towards the band, Kelly.

00:10:59.124 --> 00:11:00.492
I mean, she has a TV --

00:11:00.492 --> 00:11:02.561
I feel like she did that
on purpose.

00:11:07.366 --> 00:11:10.202
It is how she walks, though.
She's always very --

00:11:12.504 --> 00:11:16.475
I think they taught them that
on "American Idol."

00:11:16.475 --> 00:11:20.245
Always let people
just see the front.

00:11:20.245 --> 00:11:21.646
[ Clears throat ]

00:11:21.646 --> 00:11:24.649
Oh, New Year's resolution.

00:11:24.649 --> 00:11:26.352
We're right near the end.

00:11:28.487 --> 00:11:30.455
Yeah.

00:11:30.455 --> 00:11:33.358
Uh, New Year's resolution
was I'm going to

00:11:33.358 --> 00:11:35.961
stop biting my nails.

00:11:35.961 --> 00:11:40.399
So let's take a quick check in
and see how I'm doing.

00:11:40.399 --> 00:11:41.534
-[ Screams ]

00:11:41.534 --> 00:11:43.069
-Seven days.

00:11:49.241 --> 00:11:52.011
Ah, well.

00:11:52.011 --> 00:11:53.646
That's about it.

00:11:55.947 --> 00:11:59.250
I don't regret the one
I didn't do.

00:11:59.250 --> 00:12:03.022
In general, you know,

00:12:03.022 --> 00:12:04.889
I just deal the cards I'm dealt.

00:12:04.889 --> 00:12:07.526
That's how you say it.
That's the expression, right?

00:12:10.362 --> 00:12:15.668
I realized why I stopped
getting invited to poker nights.

00:12:15.668 --> 00:12:19.438
They'd deal me cards, and then
I would just deal them back.

00:12:22.908 --> 00:12:25.477
You got to deal
the cards you're dealt.

00:12:25.477 --> 00:12:30.149
No, man. You don't.
You got to play them.

00:12:30.149 --> 00:12:31.817
Not what my daddy taught me.

00:12:31.817 --> 00:12:33.452
Mm.

00:12:36.555 --> 00:12:37.757
See me next week.

